{"clock":3,"ops":[{"kind":"link","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","forge_id":"5958448221","number":"32","url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/32"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","field":"title","value":"bridge: a failed repository check after a not-found marks a bug gone"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","field":"body","value":"Found in the native-fields final review; it predates native-fields. In both adapters, `confirm()` (bridge/github/remote.go, bridge/gitlab/remote.go) checks the repository after a write or read answers \"not found\". When that check fails too, `confirm()` wraps the original not-found, and the engine marks the bug gone for good: every later pull and push skips it.\n\nFix: when the repository check fails, return its own error, not the not-found, so the bug stays synced and the run reports the failure. Add a test with a reader that can't see the repository.\n"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","field":"status","value":"open"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","field":"labels","value":"kind:bug\nprio:p2\nstatus:backlog"}},{"kind":"seen","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1793004401,"data":{"issue":"731e053ac0fe4279734369334aec110b7e9bc155","field":"assignees","value":"161889"}}]}